  "text": "We further observed that silencing PinX1 in combination with radioimmunotherapy markedly promoted M1 macrophage polarization in NSCLC. Macrophages constitute a major component of the TIME in lung cancer [51]. Macrophages exist in two principal phenotypes: pro-inflammatory (M1-type) macrophages and anti-inflammatory (M2-type) macrophages [52]. M1-type macrophages kill tumor cells either directly, through cytotoxicity, or indirectly, through antibody-dependent cellular cytotoxicity, whereas pro-tumorigenic M2-type macrophages instead support tumor growth, invasion and metastasis [52]. Reprogramming tumor-associated macrophages from the M2 to the M1 phenotype is therefore critical for alleviating the immunosuppressive state of the TIME and restraining tumor growth. Beyond the induction of ICD, optimized radiotherapy can itself promote the conversion of M2 to M1 macrophages within the TIME [53]. Collectively, these findings help explain why targeting PinX1 can shift the tumor microenvironment toward a more immunostimulatory, tumor-suppressive state."
}

